    "script": "Launching a support bot for Black Friday? Here are the 5 moments it has to hand the customer to a person. An apparel brand we work with in Berlin lets AI answer 72 in 100 support tickets in 4 languages. The other 28 go to a person, on purpose. An angry customer. Someone who wants to cancel. A refund over your limit. A question the bot isn't sure about. And anyone who asks for a human. Skip these and people stop trusting the bot. With a human option, 55 in 100 trust AI to fix their issue. Without one, just 26. And that Berlin brand? It still saves 1 in 4 customers who try to cancel. Comment SYSTEMS and we'll send you the full handoff map.",
